# sha256 of every source this package downloads.
#
# Checked by scripts/verify-sources.sh on every build, local and in COPR, and
# again in CI against a fresh download — which is what would catch the tag
# being moved upstream after the fact.
#
# Verified with `make check-sources PACKAGE=gaffer`, not `sha256sum -c`: the
# comments here are deliberate and coreutils rejects them.
#
# gaffer 0.2.2 — tag v0.2.2, commit e566af00ffda925c0366eaa1be45153e465a2992.
# The commit is recorded so a moved tag can be identified, not just detected.
# This tag is signed and, upstream, immutable — but that is a promise made by
# the forge, and this file is what checks it from the outside.
8d9522d3195684dc7bbe1eddad5232062d6d4e5646ac5522e27ef7fe666a42dd  gaffer-0.2.2.tar.gz
